# Land Rover Discovery 4 five-door, 2009-2016.
#
# The fourth Discovery: the Discovery 3 shell with the smoother nose, the
# new lamps, the more powerful engines and the revised interior. The
# five-door is modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Land_Rover_Discovery
#
# Dimensions 4.838 x 2.022 m (with mirrors folded) x 1.970 m (including roof
# rails), wheelbase 2.885 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is the side profile; the front and rear
# three-quarters show the lamps, grille and tailgate.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the Land Rover Discovery 4 UK brochure for the 2013
# model year (LRML 3983/12): Fuji White, Santorini Black, Indus Silver and
# Aintree Green. Weights 15, 13, 12, 10, total 50, provisional.
#
# Speed 195 km/h. Comfort 90/465, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 90. Class 3.
# Dates are road presence: 2009 intro, retires staggered 2031-2034.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/land-rover-discovery-4.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/land-rover-discovery-4.dae. References:
# citycars/references/land-rover-discovery-4/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: there is no true profile, so the flank is estimated. The
# rear quarter glass is a rectangular panel, the arch cladding is a flat ribbon,
# and the model's body is 1.95 m wide with mirrors reaching 2.02 m to stay within
# the tile. At 128 px the L319 shell, deeper bumper and mesh grille read as a
# Discovery 4, though it is close to the Discovery 3 from the side.


obj=citycar
name=LandRoverDiscovery4(FujiWhite)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=15
intro_year=2009
intro_month=9
retire_year=2034
retire_month=6
speed=195
class=3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=90
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=465

